{"result":{"api_status":null,"cache":{},"canonical_url":"https://github.com/antiwork/gumroad-cli","error_class":null,"http_status":200,"item_ids":["github:antiwork/gumroad-cli@806dfc0a4bf13585a548652f8919c3dc4089695c"],"payload":{"latest_commit":{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265388744?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gumclaw","id":265388744,"login":"gumclaw","node_id":"U_kgDOD9GCyA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gumclaw","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/antiwork/gumroad-cli/commits/806dfc0a4bf13585a548652f8919c3dc4089695c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T18:35:01Z","email":"gumclaw@gumroad.com","name":"gumclaw"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T18:35:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Scale sales refund --amount by the sale's own currency (#193)\n\n* Scale sales refund --amount by the sale's own currency\n\nParseMoney was called with an empty currency, so it always multiplied by\n100. On a JPY-listed sale --amount 25 requested a 2500 yen refund and the\nserver accepted it whenever the refundable balance allowed, with the\nconfirmation prompt echoing the wrong figure too.\n\nA partial refund now looks the sale up first to read its currency, refuses\nrather than guessing when it cannot, and labels the amount it echoes.\n\nRefs gumroad-private#1782\n\n* Validate --amount syntax before the sale lookup in sales refund\n\nGreptile flagged that a malformed --amount (abc, negative) triggered\nan authenticated GET before local validation, so a bad lookup/auth\nerror masked the actionable input error and burned a request.\n\n* Fix dry-run and test-routing gaps found in review of #193\n\nFetchRequestDecoded had no --dry-run guard, so a future mutating caller\nwould make a real request under --dry-run instead of refusing. Refund's\nown dry-run path still works: it goes through the GET lookup (needed to\npreview the scaled amount) and only the PUT is short-circuited.\n\nAlso route the sales-refund test double on HTTP method instead of a\npath suffix, since a sale id ending in \"refund\" defeated the old\nsuffix match, and add a --json envelope test for the partial-refund path.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: gumclaw <gumclaw@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"11cadaf3271039d92694faa3b486aff615482fef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/antiwork/gumroad-cli/git/trees/11cadaf3271039d92694faa3b486aff615482fef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/antiwork/gumroad-cli/git/commits/806dfc0a4bf13585a548652f8919c3dc4089695c","verification":{"payload":"tree 11cadaf3271039d92694faa3b486aff615482fef\nparent f7d0fbdf012fecf2e3426890b9b192866d3928f1\nauthor gumclaw <gumclaw@gumroad.com> 1785782101 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785782101 -0400\n\nScale sales refund --amount by the sale's own currency (#193)\n\n* Scale sales refund --amount by the sale's own currency\n\nParseMoney was called with an empty currency, so it always multiplied by\n100. On a JPY-listed sale --amount 25 requested a 2500 yen refund and the\nserver accepted it whenever the refundable balance allowed, with the\nconfirmation prompt echoing the wrong figure too.\n\nA partial refund now looks the sale up first to read its currency, refuses\nrather than guessing when it cannot, and labels the amount it echoes.\n\nRefs gumroad-private#1782\n\n* Validate --amount syntax before the sale lookup in sales refund\n\nGreptile flagged that a malformed --amount (abc, negative) triggered\nan authenticated GET before local validation, so a bad lookup/auth\nerror masked the actionable input error and burned a request.\n\n* Fix dry-run and test-routing gaps found in review of #193\n\nFetchRequestDecoded had no --dry-run guard, so a future mutating caller\nwould make a real request under --dry-run instead of refusing. Refund's\nown dry-run path still works: it goes through the GET lookup (needed to\npreview the scaled amount) and only the PUT is short-circuited.\n\nAlso route the sales-refund test double on HTTP method instead of a\npath suffix, since a sale id ending in \"refund\" defeated the old\nsuffix match, and add a --json envelope test for the partial-refund path.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: gumclaw <gumclaw@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcN9VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/1MQAFdrgZ06DxGu4Kbio6FO7F2t\nWSHX4JuOIRIWBiPV0mDQdJ4KTKpPj2o/Jf5tIzxbIqh0sGpXAB/ZPL8TEbI88XO1\n56KMdLHdwaX/nB0WPDfkjFg6qAe74k9mn+JOir/5+R77fi8glZsyM7rc9GcG1SQ8\nt4GEuBNOTLH940VYm+IGclfAOwUKY1u/U1nYAARpiLWG0m9CcE8kVjRjhssQezLs\nxZjT7zCNAWfm7bT/4cYCeuO0oTgUv6/DRgji6hyLv8cD7dgvqMwZXN2L5PVtWctr\n2FKHKmVg5P9JigaEQHLphWz6BdZuByT0hk++uKVWLU49DW0blb9S+66atASYsm5H\nxH8jjG2pw1w6D62JsIv2N7Q9Au+sGhIvDYnr89PTXeRK2oPrcSvurTPpgzXFfb3p\nuzWFsey8tQlXLc4SQf+FstjLO9k1xoBbELfBeFMFFNkS2oB+OJam6CnGeByR7xHl\nn7upjTdycl0kPdsIxzlwbcLiq2asopqRfIgD299ThgDVwdiBxuoqqs/Pv4bmG81S\nTvD3cp53xCDGMMyGaF3xj9aBeXmuQOZEuoQkM8OVg61fX0EOeBvSGBvG/0ToU571\nPQVQWpL02fBAcKePUZ5A3AXXzT7tvePWq/Wx6tNwO0lQmVi2YMOAtlZOdvzUPRmV\naKavyQfSVlpR27ZZQADu\n=49Ci\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T18:40:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://